{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Nginx on node1 serves a successful HTTP response at / on TCP port 6500.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct checks before and after node restart show nginx active and enabled, listening on IPv4 and IPv6 port 6500, and returning HTTP/1.1 200 with the configured page at the node's managed IP. The complete restart protocol also demonstrates persistence and recovery: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service and content.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f9203d63dc814e55","cmd-51a03547e61a49e5","cmd-6ea557c634f74f7e","cmd-a8963db301bc4688","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"The implementation was focused and left package state healthy with no failed services. Two retained hygiene issues are visible: enabling the packaged nginx configuration also left nginx listening unnecessarily on TCP 80, outside the requested port 6500; and the mandatory restart command left /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log behind. The restart itself was required evidence collection, but its temporary log was not cleaned up. No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b262cba78120445c","cmd-51a03547e61a49e5","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is satisfied with strong direct behavioral evidence, including successful HTTP 200 responses on port 6500 before and after a fully evidenced node restart. Minor hygiene deductions apply for the unintended port 80 listener and an abandoned restart log.","limitations":["HTTP behavior was tested from node1 to its own managed IP rather than from a separate client, so end-to-end reachability from another host was not directly observed.","The evidence does not show whether firewalld permits the unintended TCP 80 listener, so the degree of external exposure is uncertain."]}
